---
export const prerender = true;
import GifcitiesLayout from '../../layouts/GifcitiesLayout.astro';
---
<GifcitiesLayout
  title="Support — GifCities for iMessage"
  description="FAQ and support contact for GifCities for iMessage."
>
  <h1>support</h1>

  <h2>how do I enable the extension?</h2>
  <p>
    Open Messages, start a conversation, and tap the App Store icon (grey circle with an "A")
    next to the text field to open the app drawer. Tap the GifCities icon to launch it.
    If you don't see it, tap the ••• "More" button in the drawer, tap "Edit", and switch
    GifCities on.
  </p>

  <h2>why might a GIF fail to load?</h2>
  <p>
    GIFs are fetched live from the Internet Archive's servers, not stored in the app.
    Some archived files are slow to load or occasionally unavailable. If one doesn't load,
    try again in a moment or pick a different result.
  </p>

  <h2>how do I report an issue?</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:hudbud@gmail.com">hudbud@gmail.com</a>, or open an issue on
    <a href="https://github.com/hudbud/gifcities-imessage">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</GifcitiesLayout>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 20px; text-align: center; }
  h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 22px 0 6px; }
  h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  p { max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto; }
</style>
